- [Crow] (laughing) Isn't that cute,

1008
00:41:30,206 --> 00:41:33,332
he's trying to tell us something!

1009
00:41:33,332 --> 00:41:34,165
- [Tom] Can we play through?

1010
00:41:34,165 --> 00:41:35,203
We got a hot one back here.

1011
00:41:35,203 --> 00:41:36,456
- You wanna hold this?

1012
00:41:36,456 --> 00:41:38,827
I gotta go call headquarters.

1013
00:41:38,827 --> 00:41:42,410
- [Joel] That Merlin
is lost without a map.

1014
00:41:43,938 --> 00:41:46,098
- [Crow] Don't laugh,
you're only encouraging him.

1015
00:41:46,098 --> 00:41:49,784
- [Joel] (laughing) Mitchell, oh.

1016
00:41:49,784 --> 00:41:51,699
(ominous music)

1017
00:41:51,699 --> 00:41:52,938
- [Tom] The new Chrysler Fury,

1018
00:41:52,938 --> 00:41:56,342
the car that thinks it's a house.

1019
00:41:56,342 --> 00:41:57,175
- [Joel] I can't believe it,

1020
00:41:57,175 --> 00:41:58,008
I'm in trouble for killing us a civilian.

1021
00:41:58,008 --> 00:42:00,001
- Mitchell, I thought
your job was Cummings.

1022
00:42:00,001 --> 00:42:00,995
- I've been busy.

1023
00:42:00,995 --> 00:42:01,921
- Oh really?

1024
00:42:01,921 --> 00:42:04,021
- Yeah, you think I would
have (Mitchell mumbling)

1025
00:42:04,021 --> 00:42:06,369
- Nope, you may be facing
a disciplinary charge

1026
00:42:06,369 --> 00:42:07,415
for shooting him.

1027
00:42:07,415 --> 00:42:09,278
- What the hell, you wanted
him for two weeks, no bail,

1028
00:42:09,278 --> 00:42:10,684
that's how you got him.

1029
00:42:10,684 --> 00:42:12,598
- I didn't expect you to shoot him.

1030
00:42:12,598 --> 00:42:14,451
- Oh you were asking that, Aldridge.

1031
00:42:14,451 --> 00:42:16,334
- [Crow] I thought I
had authority over him!

1032
00:42:16,334 --> 00:42:18,522
- [Cummings] You shouldn't have
blown your cover like that.

1033
00:42:18,522 --> 00:42:20,440
I'll go phone headquarters.

1034
00:42:20,440 --> 00:42:22,455
- [Tom] Pass the potatoes,
the peas, the butter,

1035
00:42:22,455 --> 00:42:24,221
the peas, the pie, the butter.

1036
00:42:24,221 --> 00:42:26,981
(man talking)

1037
00:42:26,981 --> 00:42:29,104
Oh trouble, oh pass the
gravy, the stuffing.

1038
00:42:29,104 --> 00:42:31,437
- Don't forget Mr. Mitchell.

1039
00:42:33,390 --> 00:42:37,617
- [Joel] (spitting)
Oh, that's one of mine.

1040
00:42:37,617 --> 00:42:41,971
- [Crow] This is the part
of being a henchman I hate.

1041
00:42:41,971 --> 00:42:44,663
- [Tom] Can I tempt you with some dessert?

1042
00:42:44,663 --> 00:42:46,850
- I don't think Benton likes you.

1043
00:42:46,850 --> 00:42:50,250
- [Joel] Uh, can we get more
volume on that jacket please?

1044
00:42:50,250 --> 00:42:53,640
- That's the trouble, not
too many people like you.

1045
00:42:53,640 --> 00:42:55,894
You ought to cultivate
people, go out to them.

1046
00:42:55,894 --> 00:42:57,214
With your confidence, you never know

1047
00:42:57,214 --> 00:42:58,618
when they're gonna come in useful.

1048
00:42:58,618 --> 00:42:59,557
You've gotta be nice to them.

1049
00:42:59,557 --> 00:43:01,649
- [Tom] Oh, nice, more butter please.

1050
00:43:01,649 --> 00:43:04,024
- Well what about the
heroin, Mr. Cummings?

1051
00:43:04,024 --> 00:43:05,193
- Forget the heroin.

1052
00:43:05,193 --> 00:43:06,121
- [Joel] That's for dessert!

1053
00:43:06,121 --> 00:43:08,070
- Don't talk about the
heroin over the soup.

1054
00:43:08,070 --> 00:43:09,900
That's your trouble, you're impatient.

1055
00:43:09,900 --> 00:43:12,452
Now you're aware that guy
Zippy's gonna do some harm.

1056
00:43:12,452 --> 00:43:14,185
- I wanted to find out who he was.

1057
00:43:14,185 --> 00:43:17,312
- Well ask him, don't shoot him.

1058
00:43:17,312 --> 00:43:18,145
Who was he?

1059
00:43:18,145 --> 00:43:21,239
- [Tom] Well I didn't ask him, I shot him.

1060
00:43:21,239 --> 00:43:22,832
- Uh, Booker, got Booker.

1061
00:43:22,832 --> 00:43:24,213
- [Crow] Booker's a good cop!

1062
00:43:24,213 --> 00:43:26,044
- Booker, Booker, Booker?

1063
00:43:26,044 --> 00:43:26,924
- [Tom] Who's got the Booker?

1064
00:43:26,924 --> 00:43:28,848
- No, Bocca, with a double C.

1065
00:43:28,848 --> 00:43:30,015
Edmundo Bocca.

1066
00:43:31,404 --> 00:43:32,748
- Like the soup?

1067
00:43:32,748 --> 00:43:36,082
- [Crow] Goes with my pie.
- [Mitchell] Yes.

1068
00:43:36,082 --> 00:43:37,043
You got this place laid out

1069
00:43:37,043 --> 00:43:38,730
like a real banquet, Mr. Cummings.

1070
00:43:38,730 --> 00:43:40,548
- For a business dinner.

1071
00:43:40,548 --> 00:43:42,572
We might talk business later.

1072
00:43:42,572 --> 00:43:44,292
Can I have some more soup, Benton?

1073
00:43:44,292 --> 00:43:46,282
- There is no more soup, sir.

1074
00:43:46,282 --> 00:43:47,481
- [Joel] I sense he's lying,

1075
00:43:47,481 --> 00:43:48,390
but why would he lie about the soup?

1076
00:43:48,390 --> 00:43:51,690
- How do you like that, in
my own house, no more soup.

1077
00:43:51,690 --> 00:43:53,805
- [Tom] My dinner with Mitchell.

1078
00:43:53,805 --> 00:43:56,313
- Bocca works for Mistretta.

1079
00:43:56,313 --> 00:43:57,339
- That's the first piece of information

1080
00:43:57,339 --> 00:43:59,139
you've come up with, Mr. Cummings.

1081
00:43:59,139 --> 00:44:01,827
- [Crow] How 'bout letting us in on some?

1082
00:44:01,827 --> 00:44:03,235
- Benton, what are you
doing with those steaks,

1083
00:44:03,235 --> 00:44:04,718
are you growing them?

1084
00:44:04,718 --> 00:44:08,755
- [Tom] (laughing sarcastically)
You can't grow steaks.

1085
00:44:08,755 --> 00:44:12,172
- [Crow] Oh wait, I want the bone marrow.

1086
00:44:13,056 --> 00:44:14,653
- [Joel] Oh, boom mike, big time, whoo.

1087
00:44:14,653 --> 00:44:16,788
- You gonna take all
night peeling that orange?

1088
00:44:16,788 --> 00:44:20,955
- I thought maybe we might
talk about the shipment.

1089
00:44:23,421 --> 00:44:27,004
- [Tom] Would you just
give me that orange?

1090
00:44:28,119 --> 00:44:30,536
- [Crow] I have a new friend.

1091
00:44:32,481 --> 00:44:34,368
- [Joel] Uh hey, I put a
couple rolls in my pocket,

1092
00:44:34,368 --> 00:44:35,451
is that okay?

1093
00:44:37,521 --> 00:44:38,747
- What I want to know is--

1094
00:44:38,747 --> 00:44:41,080
- The coffee's cold, Benton,
you're a lousy butler.

1095
00:44:41,080 --> 00:44:41,913
- [Benton] I am not a lousy butler!

1096
00:44:41,913 --> 00:44:43,281
- You're a lousy butler.

1097
00:44:43,281 --> 00:44:44,443
- I am not.

1098
00:44:44,443 --> 00:44:46,981
- I say you're a lousy
butler, the coffee is cold.

1099
00:44:46,981 --> 00:44:47,814
- [Mitchell] Well I think I gotta go.

1100
00:44:47,814 --> 00:44:50,815
- [Tom] It’s "The
Servant" by Harold Pinter.

1101
00:44:50,815 --> 00:44:54,315
- [Joel] Oh look, you made Mitchell leave.

1102
00:45:01,234 --> 00:45:02,699
- [Tom] Oh man, I'm so hungry.

1103
00:45:02,699 --> 00:45:05,167
Only two steaks for dinner,
didn't get to finish my orange.

1104
00:45:05,167 --> 00:45:09,000
All the frozen yogurt
places were closed, ugh.

1105
00:45:09,981 --> 00:45:11,877
Big buttery moon up there,

1106
00:45:11,877 --> 00:45:15,149
sidewalk kind of looks like
ice cream if you squint hard.

1107
00:45:15,149 --> 00:45:16,982
Stairs look like cake.

1108
00:45:18,029 --> 00:45:19,315
- [Joel] Mitchell's legions of fans

1109
00:45:19,315 --> 00:45:22,648
show up at any time of the day or night.

1110
00:45:25,344 --> 00:45:29,427
- [Crow] Well, this'll be
okay, I don't see, oof!

1111
00:45:30,865 --> 00:45:34,140
- [Joel] Jeez, those Jehovah’s
Witnesses are getting tough!

1112
00:45:34,140 --> 00:45:35,223
- [Tom] Whoa.

1113
00:45:36,573 --> 00:45:37,613
Now they're gonna end up with

1114
00:45:37,613 --> 00:45:39,213
Mitchell's dinner all over them.

1115
00:45:39,213 --> 00:45:40,616
(men struggling)

1116
00:45:40,616 --> 00:45:42,773
Oh wait, hold it, a little piece of bacon.

1117
00:45:42,773 --> 00:45:45,287
(men struggling)

1118
00:45:45,287 --> 00:45:47,146
- [Joel] You know is it wrong
for me to want to see this?

1119
00:45:47,146 --> 00:45:48,603
- [Crow] Uh, nope.

1120
00:45:48,603 --> 00:45:51,775
- [Tom] Ooh, right in the
tenderloin steak region.

1121
00:45:51,775 --> 00:45:55,942
- [Crow] Oh, sorry bud, we
thought you were Rockford.

1122
00:45:56,891 --> 00:46:01,074
- [Tom] Oh, I think this
is rice, oh, no it's not.

1123
00:46:01,074 --> 00:46:01,907
(laughing)

1124
00:46:01,907 --> 00:46:03,550
- [Joel] Well, ol’
Mitchell sure got his self

1125
00:46:03,550 --> 00:46:05,530
hogtied and railroaded there.

1126
00:46:05,530 --> 00:46:08,443
♫ My my my my Mitchell

1127
00:46:08,443 --> 00:46:10,783
♫ What would your mama say ♫

1128
00:46:10,783 --> 00:46:11,616
(man talking under sheets)

1129
00:46:11,616 --> 00:46:14,105
- [Crow] Oh, he's alone reading
a comic book under there.

1130
00:46:14,105 --> 00:46:16,688
(upbeat music)

1131
00:46:19,599 --> 00:46:21,057
- [Tom] Mitchell honey, do you have any

1132
00:46:21,057 --> 00:46:22,807
new age or something?

1133
00:46:25,711 --> 00:46:29,461
- [Joel] Oh, he's sleeping
with Helen Keller.

1134
00:46:33,125 --> 00:46:37,446
- [Crow] Oh, how I long for
"The Burning Bed" right now.

1135
00:46:37,446 --> 00:46:41,379
- [Tom] You got a lot of junk around here.

1136
00:46:41,379 --> 00:46:46,205
♫ Well oh my my my Mitchell ♫

1137
00:46:46,205 --> 00:46:47,491
- [Crow] Why would anyone want

1138
00:46:47,491 --> 00:46:48,777
to do this with Mitchell, Joel?

1139
00:46:48,777 --> 00:46:49,860
- [Joel] Shh.

1140
00:46:52,271 --> 00:46:53,938
A vase or two faces?

1141
00:47:02,049 --> 00:47:04,192
- [Tom] Oh Yanni, I mean
John, I mean Mitchell!

1142
00:47:04,192 --> 00:47:07,109
♫ Oh my my my Mitchell

1143
00:47:07,109 --> 00:47:09,866
♫ You shoot 'em just to get 'em in jail ♫

1144
00:47:09,866 --> 00:47:11,314
- [Joel] Hey watch this,
I learned this in college,

1145
00:47:11,314 --> 00:47:12,147
check this out, beer cans.

1146
00:47:12,147 --> 00:47:13,952
- [Tom] That's class.

1147
00:47:13,952 --> 00:47:16,780
(mimicking can opening and chugging)

1148
00:47:16,780 --> 00:47:17,684
- [Joel] Baby oil!

1149
00:47:17,684 --> 00:47:20,351
(all screaming)

1150
00:47:22,900 --> 00:47:26,148
(Tom throwing up)

1151
00:47:26,148 --> 00:47:30,315
♫ My my my God, no ♫

1152
00:47:32,801 --> 00:47:34,773
- [Joel] Could you maybe
get aroused, Mitchell?

1153
00:47:34,773 --> 00:47:35,738
(Joel trails off)

1154
00:47:35,738 --> 00:47:37,014
(robots crying)

1155
00:47:37,014 --> 00:47:38,931
Um, how about some BTO?

1156
00:47:44,517 --> 00:47:46,366
- You went through that Tuesday.

1157
00:47:46,366 --> 00:47:47,798
- [Tom] And I still
don't have any Tic Tacs.

1158
00:47:47,798 --> 00:47:49,715
- But this is Thursday.

1159
00:47:52,093 --> 00:47:54,676
- [Crow] He makes a good point.

1160
00:47:56,978 --> 00:47:57,811
(sighing)

1161
00:47:57,811 --> 00:47:59,680
- You're gonna get busted for this.

1162
00:47:59,680 --> 00:48:02,198
- Guy that busted me would
have to be very straight.

1163
00:48:02,198 --> 00:48:03,894
- You implying that I'm not straight?

1164
00:48:03,894 --> 00:48:04,727
(Joel laughing)

1165
00:48:04,727 --> 00:48:07,644
- [Joel] You're boozy, but lovable.

1166
00:48:08,549 --> 00:48:10,982
(woman mumbling)

1167
00:48:10,982 --> 00:48:13,225
- The only trouble is you don't know it.

1168
00:48:13,225 --> 00:48:16,854
- You really think I'd take
some sort of a payoff, huh?

1169
00:48:16,854 --> 00:48:19,022
- You already have, haven't you?

1170
00:48:19,022 --> 00:48:20,815
- Oh wait a minute.

1171
00:48:20,815 --> 00:48:22,390
So you're a Christmas gift.

1172
00:48:22,390 --> 00:48:23,223
- [Crow] And I wanted a Super Soaker.

1173
00:48:23,223 --> 00:48:24,274
- That's what you said.

1174
00:48:24,274 --> 00:48:25,422
- Did I?
- [Mitchell] Didn't you?

1175
00:48:25,422 --> 00:48:27,012
Damn right.

1176
00:48:27,012 --> 00:48:29,206
That doesn't make me the cooperative type.

1177
00:48:29,206 --> 00:48:31,113
You just watch your pretty mouth.

1178
00:48:31,113 --> 00:48:32,859
- So bust me.

1179
00:48:32,859 --> 00:48:35,584
You're a policeman and that's grass.

1180
00:48:35,584 --> 00:48:37,590
- [Crow] Merlin Olsen
sent him that painting.

1181
00:48:37,590 --> 00:48:38,986
(laughing)

1182
00:48:38,986 --> 00:48:40,282
- [Joel] My Mitchell,
I think I'll keep him.

1183
00:48:40,282 --> 00:48:42,115
- [Greta] Oh, come on.

1184
00:48:43,009 --> 00:48:43,842
Come on.

1185
00:48:45,263 --> 00:48:46,263
- [Crow] Ew.

1186
00:48:47,601 --> 00:48:49,847
Are they done, can I look?

1187
00:48:49,847 --> 00:48:52,241
- You sure know how to bring a girl down.

1188
00:48:52,241 --> 00:48:55,909
- [Tom] Double room please, one night.

1189
00:48:55,909 --> 00:48:57,642
- He sleeps with me then busts me.

1190
00:48:57,642 --> 00:48:58,788
- [Crow] First things first!

1191
00:48:58,788 --> 00:49:00,193
- Well she asked me to.

1192
00:49:00,193 --> 00:49:03,673
- What, sleep with her or bust her?

1193
00:49:03,673 --> 00:49:04,540
- Both.

1194
00:49:04,540 --> 00:49:06,165
(Joel mimicking a sad trombone)

1195
00:49:06,165 --> 00:49:07,539
(officer talking)

1196
00:49:07,539 --> 00:49:09,727
- When your case is heard,

1197
00:49:09,727 --> 00:49:11,809
are there any other offenses you'd like

1198
00:49:11,809 --> 00:49:14,175
for us to take into consideration

1199
00:49:14,175 --> 00:49:16,455
while you're in this kind of a mood?

1200
00:49:16,455 --> 00:49:19,474
- Yeah, being hung up on this guy.

1201
00:49:19,474 --> 00:49:21,221
- That's a mistake, lady.

1202
00:49:21,221 --> 00:49:22,054
- [Tom] Didn't do me any good.

1203
00:49:22,054 --> 00:49:23,471
- Not an offense.

1204
00:49:24,307 --> 00:49:25,687
- When can I see my lawyer?

1205
00:49:25,687 --> 00:49:27,197
- We'll take care of it for you.

1206
00:49:27,197 --> 00:49:28,522
- [Joel] You're sleeping
with him at three.

1207
00:49:28,522 --> 00:49:30,507
(police officer talking)

1208
00:49:30,507 --> 00:49:33,661
- Hey, that's only a $500 fine.

1209
00:49:33,661 --> 00:49:36,035
For $1,000 a night, you're still a hit.

1210
00:49:36,035 --> 00:49:37,003
- [Crow] Not after taxes.

1211
00:49:37,003 --> 00:49:38,709
- Oh, you're a terrific human being.

1212
00:49:38,709 --> 00:49:40,964
I had a clean record in this town.

1213
00:49:40,964 --> 00:49:42,738
- [Tom] Sirens!

1214
00:49:42,738 --> 00:49:43,571
- Hey.

1215
00:49:45,637 --> 00:49:48,832
- Make sure she signs
the property receipt.

1216
00:49:48,832 --> 00:49:50,418
- [Crow] Nobody asked for a prostitute,

1217
00:49:50,418 --> 00:49:52,178
we can take her right away!

1218
00:49:52,178 --> 00:49:55,214
- [Joel] Are we still on for Tuesday?

1219
00:49:55,214 --> 00:49:56,047
- Hey.

1220
00:49:56,950 --> 00:49:58,424
You really sleep with her?

1221
00:49:58,424 --> 00:49:59,512
- Yep.

1222
00:49:59,512 --> 00:50:02,095
- [Crow] And then I kissed her.

1223
00:50:04,822 --> 00:50:07,518
- [Tom] Hey Wally.
- [Crow] Mitch.

1224
00:50:07,518 --> 00:50:08,351
(car honking)

1225
00:50:08,351 --> 00:50:10,726
- [Joel] At Beneficial
you're good for more.

1226
00:50:10,726 --> 00:50:13,064
(car honking)

1227
00:50:13,064 --> 00:50:14,710
- [Tom] The declining years of Lee Majors.

1228
00:50:14,710 --> 00:50:16,870
- Ask him to come in.

1229
00:50:16,870 --> 00:50:19,485
Say that it's important,
say that I have to see him.

1230
00:50:19,485 --> 00:50:20,385
- Yes sir.

1231
00:50:20,385 --> 00:50:23,468
- [Crow] Tell him we have sour cream.

1232
00:50:28,204 --> 00:50:32,865
- [Joel] Oh man, this
stakeout's getting crowded.

1233
00:50:32,865 --> 00:50:34,282
- [Tom] Hi folks.

1234
00:50:37,083 --> 00:50:40,000
- [Crow] Duh, the steaks are ready.

1235
00:50:40,983 --> 00:50:43,233
- [Tom] Can Linda come too?

1236
00:50:45,727 --> 00:50:49,894
- [Joel] So tell me Merlin,
do you know Roman Gabriel?

1237
00:50:51,605 --> 00:50:54,265
- [Crow] I think you're a good butler.

1238
00:50:54,265 --> 00:50:55,997
♫ Movin' on up ♫

1239
00:50:55,997 --> 00:50:57,565
- [Tom] Weezy!

1240
00:50:57,565 --> 00:51:00,398
- This way.
- [Joel] To Wall Drug.

1241
00:51:02,374 --> 00:51:03,207
- You want a drink?

1242
00:51:03,207 --> 00:51:04,455
- [Joel] Is the Pope Catholic?

1243
00:51:04,455 --> 00:51:05,592
- [Cummings] Sit down.

1244
00:51:05,592 --> 00:51:09,030
- [Crow] Wanna shoot a beer bong?

1245
00:51:09,030 --> 00:51:10,837
- Alright, Mitchell.

1246
00:51:10,837 --> 00:51:12,269
Why don't we stop messing around.

1247
00:51:12,269 --> 00:51:13,382
- What's that gonna mean?

1248
00:51:13,382 --> 00:51:14,950
- I wanna put you on the payroll.

1249
00:51:14,950 --> 00:51:16,061
- [Tom] We have an opening in retail.

1250
00:51:16,061 --> 00:51:17,166
- I'm in trouble.

1251
00:51:17,166 --> 00:51:19,569
You sensed it, you know it, and I know it.

1252
00:51:19,569 --> 00:51:21,608
- Specifically what trouble?

1253
00:51:21,608 --> 00:51:22,834
- Well, the idea of the payroll,

1254
00:51:22,834 --> 00:51:24,282
now I get to ask the questions.

1255
00:51:24,282 --> 00:51:25,986
- [Tom] Noted.

1256
00:51:25,986 --> 00:51:27,355
- I need help.

1257
00:51:27,355 --> 00:51:28,829
- [Joel] I've got a
purple mole on my back.

1258
00:51:28,829 --> 00:51:30,997
- I need help from any
source that I can get it.

1259
00:51:30,997 --> 00:51:31,830
- [Crow] So I'm down to you.

1260
00:51:31,830 --> 00:51:33,217
- Well put it on the line.

1261
00:51:33,217 --> 00:51:34,808
- I wanna buy your services.

1262
00:51:34,808 --> 00:51:36,456
Your voice on the phone in case I need

1263
00:51:36,456 --> 00:51:38,866
the help of your police department.

1264
00:51:38,866 --> 00:51:40,658
- Let me just uh, write the details

1265
00:51:40,658 --> 00:51:43,324
of your bribe down, Mr. Cummings.

1266
00:51:43,324 --> 00:51:45,345
- [Joel] It's a Shriner car!

1267
00:51:45,345 --> 00:51:46,178
- [Crow] Oh, a place in the shade!

1268
00:51:46,178 --> 00:51:49,178
(cars bumping)
Ooh!

1269
00:51:53,585 --> 00:51:56,502
He pulled out right in front of me!

1270
00:51:58,856 --> 00:52:02,439
- [Joel] She's got a
David Cassidy haircut.

1271
00:52:03,484 --> 00:52:05,488
- [Crow] She's gonna write
"REDRUM" on his windshield.

1272
00:52:05,488 --> 00:52:06,571
Heh, red, oh.

1273
00:52:09,938 --> 00:52:10,872
- [Joel] He'll think of me the whole time

1274
00:52:10,872 --> 00:52:12,789
he's cleaning that off.

1275
00:52:13,893 --> 00:52:17,147
Uh, were you expecting a prostitute?

1276
00:52:17,147 --> 00:52:19,480
- [Crow] Word on the
street is you're a jerk!

1277
00:52:19,480 --> 00:52:20,679
- Could be open.

1278
00:52:20,679 --> 00:52:22,299
Cash?

1279
00:52:22,299 --> 00:52:24,521
Or subtle, just the way you
take it from other people.

1280
00:52:24,521 --> 00:52:25,985
- Uh, I don't take bribes.

1281
00:52:25,985 --> 00:52:27,251
(Tom talking over Cummings)

1282
00:52:27,251 --> 00:52:29,257
- City Hall they saw you this morning

1283
00:52:29,257 --> 00:52:32,034
with a hooker that you sleep
with and occasionally arrest.

1284
00:52:32,034 --> 00:52:33,294
- What else they tell you?

1285
00:52:33,294 --> 00:52:34,940
- She's too expensive,
you can't afford her

1286
00:52:34,940 --> 00:52:36,640
on a policeman's salary.

1287
00:52:36,640 --> 00:52:38,325
Now somebody's picking up the check.

1288
00:52:38,325 --> 00:52:40,117
Who could that be?

1289
00:52:40,117 --> 00:52:41,208
- You?

1290
00:52:41,208 --> 00:52:42,113
- Me what?

1291
00:52:42,113 --> 00:52:43,759
- You're picking up the check.

1292
00:52:43,759 --> 00:52:46,460
- No I don't, I don't pay
for your hookers Mitchell.

1293
00:52:46,460 --> 00:52:47,293
- [Tom] Well, could you?

1294
00:52:47,293 --> 00:52:48,126
- Then who is?

1295
00:52:48,126 --> 00:52:49,347
- You mean you don't know?

1296
00:52:49,347 --> 00:52:52,270
You're a cop (laughing)
and you don't know?

1297
00:52:52,270 --> 00:52:55,940
- [Tom] (laughing) No, I don't.

1298
00:52:55,940 --> 00:52:59,472
- [Crow] I specifically
came here for dinner.

1299
00:52:59,472 --> 00:53:00,432
(snapping)

1300
00:53:00,432 --> 00:53:03,640
- [Joel] Get me some
flowers pronto, Merlin.

1301
00:53:03,640 --> 00:53:07,723
- [Tom] I'm not leaving
without some tuna wiggle.

1302
00:53:18,476 --> 00:53:22,393
- [Crow] He's gotta light
him in his bald spot.

1303
00:53:26,740 --> 00:53:28,945
- [Tom] Someone to see you, sir.

1304
00:53:28,945 --> 00:53:30,667
- I knew you'd call sooner or later.

1305
00:53:30,667 --> 00:53:32,501
- [Joel] So, are you ready
to join Hair Club yet?

1306
00:53:32,501 --> 00:53:33,584
- Come on in.

1307
00:53:34,422 --> 00:53:37,755
- [Tom] Joe Don Baker, face number four.

1308
00:53:38,620 --> 00:53:42,512
- [Joel] Hey, Joe Don.
- [Crow] Hey, hey, no.

1309
00:53:42,512 --> 00:53:45,179
- Sit down.
- [Joel] Prostitute?

1310
00:53:47,382 --> 00:53:48,514
- How do you like your scotch?

1311
00:53:48,514 --> 00:53:50,681
- [Crow] Uh, by the quart.

1312
00:53:52,387 --> 00:53:53,948
- [Joel] Come on more,
come on, keep it coming,

1313
00:53:53,948 --> 00:53:56,281
I'm a big boy, that's right.

1314
00:53:57,829 --> 00:53:59,750
- [Tom] I usually take it
with a Ding Dong in it,

1315
00:53:59,750 --> 00:54:03,248
but I guess I’ll take
it neat, that’s okay.

1316
00:54:03,248 --> 00:54:04,088
- You know--

1317
00:54:04,088 --> 00:54:06,341
- [Joel] Booze is good food.

1318
00:54:06,341 --> 00:54:07,894
- [Deaney] I admire a man like you.

1319
00:54:07,894 --> 00:54:09,430
- [Crow] Not you, specifically.

1320
00:54:09,430 --> 00:54:11,180
- You take your time,

1321
00:54:12,035 --> 00:54:13,035
you're cool.

1322
00:54:14,587 --> 00:54:16,039
Yes sir.

1323
00:54:16,039 --> 00:54:17,025
- [Joel] You know he may be a bad guy,

1324
00:54:17,025 --> 00:54:19,745
but he's got a ton of gifts up there.

1325
00:54:19,745 --> 00:54:20,944
- How's the broad?

1326
00:54:20,944 --> 00:54:22,838
- That's what I came to talk about.

1327
00:54:22,838 --> 00:54:25,332
- You know what it
costs to keep you sweet?

1328
00:54:25,332 --> 00:54:27,671
A hundred bucks an hour.

1329
00:54:27,671 --> 00:54:29,735
Tells me it happens all night.

1330
00:54:29,735 --> 00:54:30,568
But you figured out,

1331
00:54:30,568 --> 00:54:33,458
that's like a thousand
bucks before breakfast.

1332
00:54:33,458 --> 00:54:34,700
- As far as I'm concerned,

1333
00:54:34,700 --> 00:54:36,525
she's just some broad
looking for a little action.

1334
00:54:36,525 --> 00:54:37,537
(laughing)

1335
00:54:37,537 --> 00:54:38,746
- You wanna see the receipts?

1336
00:54:38,746 --> 00:54:40,520
- You're wasting your money, Deaney.

1337
00:54:40,520 --> 00:54:42,199
- Let me be the judge of that.

1338
00:54:42,199 --> 00:54:44,026
- She'll lie on my bed for nothing.

1339
00:54:44,026 --> 00:54:46,718
- [Tom] Well, I guess I'll
have to talk to my accountant.

1340
00:54:46,718 --> 00:54:48,005
- You really think so?

1341
00:54:48,005 --> 00:54:50,505
- [Joel] I'm turning Japanese.

1342
00:54:53,527 --> 00:54:56,630
- [Crow] Let me show you
what I got for Christmas.

1343
00:54:56,630 --> 00:54:59,235
- I arranged a hundred
dollar company in your name.

1344
00:54:59,235 --> 00:55:00,196
- [Joel] You mean Orion?

1345
00:55:00,196 --> 00:55:03,909
- I negotiate the transfer
of a piece of real estate.

1346
00:55:03,909 --> 00:55:06,188
- [Crow] Cross to fireplace.

1347
00:55:06,188 --> 00:55:07,355
- Well let's say,

1348
00:55:07,355 --> 00:55:10,304
- [Tom] I'm Rosalind Russell.

1349
00:55:10,304 --> 00:55:11,137
- $25,000.

1350
00:55:12,154 --> 00:55:16,027
You haven't got $25,000 but
I'll get you a bank loan.

1351
00:55:16,027 --> 00:55:17,277
All legitimate.

1352
00:55:18,710 --> 00:55:22,217
The real estate you buy
will be a piece I designate

1353
00:55:22,217 --> 00:55:25,130
and you'll buy it from one
of my subsidiary companies.

1354
00:55:25,130 --> 00:55:26,434
- [Joel] Oh man, I'm so lost.
- [Deaney] Then,

1355
00:55:26,434 --> 00:55:31,120
I'll buy it off you, for
let's say, a hundred Gs.

1356
00:55:31,120 --> 00:55:35,266
That'll give you a
clear profit of $75,000.

1357
00:55:35,266 --> 00:55:38,113
And who's to say it isn't
a genuine investment?

1358
00:55:38,113 --> 00:55:39,341
- [Tom] Is that a Slim Jim?

1359
00:55:39,341 --> 00:55:40,194
Can I have that?

1360
00:55:40,194 --> 00:55:41,740
Are you done with that?

1361
00:55:41,740 --> 00:55:42,835
- [Crow] Do you open
your Christmas presents

1362
00:55:42,835 --> 00:55:44,328
on Christmas Eve or Christmas morning?

1363
00:55:44,328 --> 00:55:45,161
- Well?

1364
00:55:46,814 --> 00:55:48,106
What do you think?

1365
00:55:48,106 --> 00:55:49,660
- I'm gonna get you for that murder.

1366
00:55:49,660 --> 00:55:51,099
- [Joel] But first, merry Christmas.

1367
00:55:51,099 --> 00:55:52,465
- Or I'll die trying.

1368
00:55:52,465 --> 00:55:54,362
- You're making the biggest
mistake of your life.

1369
00:55:54,362 --> 00:55:57,862
("Love Theme from MST3K")

1370
00:56:02,518 --> 00:56:05,466
- [Joel] Yep, another
Wednesday night at Mitchell's.

1371
00:56:05,466 --> 00:56:07,737
- [Crow] Our hero, ladies and gentlemen.

1372
00:56:07,737 --> 00:56:09,565
- [Tom] And I'm still not drunk.

1373
00:56:09,565 --> 00:56:11,791
♫ Life should be ♫

1374
00:56:11,791 --> 00:56:14,518
- [Joel] Oh my goodness, I
think BJ Thomas is in his room!

1375
00:56:14,518 --> 00:56:17,101
(smarmy music)

1376
00:56:18,050 --> 00:56:19,251
(Crow slurping)

1377
00:56:19,251 --> 00:56:23,160
- [Crow] Oh yuck, I got
a cigarette in that one.

1378
00:56:23,160 --> 00:56:24,264
- [Tom] I like to top off my beer drinking

1379
00:56:24,264 --> 00:56:27,332
with another beer, it's like dessert.

1380
00:56:27,332 --> 00:56:31,259
- [Joel] It's a very special
Joe Don Baker Christmas.

1381
00:56:31,259 --> 00:56:33,159
(Crow grunting and farting)

1382
00:56:33,159 --> 00:56:34,909
- [Joel] Hey, oh hey!

1383
00:56:37,746 --> 00:56:39,271
Booze and I are buying a house together,

1384
00:56:39,271 --> 00:56:40,938
we're gonna move in.

1385
00:56:43,051 --> 00:56:43,884
- [Crow] He’s gonna strip down

1386
00:56:43,884 --> 00:56:47,113
to his underwear and watch "McQ."

1387
00:56:47,113 --> 00:56:50,946
- [Tom] Huh, wonder what
this thing does here.

1388
00:56:53,401 --> 00:56:55,564
Water, I never knew that, wow!

1389
00:56:55,564 --> 00:56:57,546
(Crow laughing)

1390
00:56:57,546 --> 00:56:59,225
- [Crow] Oh thank God for the jump cut.

1391
00:56:59,225 --> 00:57:02,036
(voices on radio)

1392
00:57:02,036 --> 00:57:03,099
(honking)

1393
00:57:03,099 --> 00:57:05,016
- [Joel] Honey, church!

1394
00:57:07,899 --> 00:57:08,732
- [Crow] Mitchell, I'm not going

1395
00:57:08,732 --> 00:57:11,251
to your folks' for Christmas!

1396
00:57:11,251 --> 00:57:14,464
- [Tom] Man, I'm still
in this Mitchell movie.

1397
00:57:14,464 --> 00:57:15,654
- [Joel] Adam Rich!

1398
00:57:15,654 --> 00:57:18,366
(Crow groaning)

1399
00:57:18,366 --> 00:57:19,199
- Hi.

1400
00:57:20,305 --> 00:57:21,779
Are you the man from the insurance?

1401
00:57:21,779 --> 00:57:22,677
- No.

1402
00:57:22,677 --> 00:57:23,818
- He came last night.

1403
00:57:23,818 --> 00:57:25,074
- Oh?

1404
00:57:25,074 --> 00:57:27,351
- My mother doesn't like you.

1405
00:57:27,351 --> 00:57:28,491
- Well I don't like your mother.

1406
00:57:28,491 --> 00:57:29,527
- Why not?

1407
00:57:29,527 --> 00:57:30,393
- [Mitchell] Why not?

1408
00:57:30,393 --> 00:57:31,472
- Yeah, why not?

1409
00:57:31,472 --> 00:57:32,393
- No, why not?

1410
00:57:32,393 --> 00:57:33,687
- Why are you repeating what I say?

1411
00:57:33,687 --> 00:57:34,520
- [Tom] Tonight on "Crossfire."

1412
00:57:34,520 --> 00:57:35,353
- [Mitchell] Why are you
repeating what I say?

1413
00:57:35,353 --> 00:57:36,186
- I'm not!

1414
00:57:36,186 --> 00:57:37,056
- Well I'm not.

1415
00:57:37,056 --> 00:57:38,122
- [Boy] You are.

1416
00:57:38,122 --> 00:57:39,037
- Buzz off.

1417
00:57:39,037 --> 00:57:40,049
- What?

1418
00:57:40,049 --> 00:57:40,882
- [Mitchell] What?

1419
00:57:40,882 --> 00:57:41,715
- What'd you say?

1420
00:57:41,715 --> 00:57:42,637
- What'd you say?

1421
00:57:42,637 --> 00:57:43,567
- [Boy] Did you say something?

1422
00:57:43,567 --> 00:57:46,025
- Did you say something?
(Tom screaming)

1423
00:57:46,025 --> 00:57:47,198
- You're lying through your teeth.

1424
00:57:47,198 --> 00:57:48,304
- You're your lying through your teeth.

1425
00:57:48,304 --> 00:57:49,350
- [Mitchell] Buzz off, huh?

1426
00:57:49,350 --> 00:57:50,183
- Buzz off!

1427
00:57:50,183 --> 00:57:51,578
- Buzz off, kid!

1428
00:57:51,578 --> 00:57:54,159
- [Crow] The inspiration
for "Cop and a Half."

1429
00:57:54,159 --> 00:57:55,272
(Mitchell yelling)

1430
00:57:55,272 --> 00:57:56,500
- [Tom] Give him a half block head start,

1431
00:57:56,500 --> 00:57:59,266
then I'm gonna mow him over.

1432
00:57:59,266 --> 00:58:01,076
- [Joel] Oh, Schlitz would
listen to me right now,

1433
00:58:01,076 --> 00:58:02,241
that’s for sure.

1434
00:58:02,241 --> 00:58:03,860
(upbeat music)

1435
00:58:03,860 --> 00:58:06,777
♫ Did you ever have to make up your mind ♫

1436
00:58:06,777 --> 00:58:08,561
- [Joel] The Loving Handful.

1437
00:58:08,561 --> 00:58:10,247
- Why don't you have me arrested?

1438
00:58:10,247 --> 00:58:11,680
- Because you want me to.

1439
00:58:11,680 --> 00:58:13,375
Nah, I don't want you
on an assault charge,

1440
00:58:13,375 --> 00:58:15,460
I want everything, I
want you and Mistretta

1441
00:58:15,460 --> 00:58:17,454
and a lead to Gallano
and the lousy heroin.

1442
00:58:17,454 --> 00:58:18,287
- [Crow] A family, a career.

1443
00:58:18,287 --> 00:58:20,801
- Maybe you'll get them.

1444
00:58:20,801 --> 00:58:23,381
I wonder if I should have
a talk with you Mitchell.

1445
00:58:23,381 --> 00:58:25,361
- I wonder if you should too, Cummings.

1446
00:58:25,361 --> 00:58:26,913
- You just gotta come in the house.

1447
00:58:26,913 --> 00:58:27,899
- No.

1448
00:58:27,899 --> 00:58:31,035
- I give you my word nothing
will happen to you in there.

1449
00:58:31,035 --> 00:58:32,704
- I'm not scared of you, open up.

1450
00:58:32,704 --> 00:58:34,068
- [Joel] But I do have to use your washer,

1451
00:58:34,068 --> 00:58:35,823
if that's alright.

1452
00:58:35,823 --> 00:58:36,666
- [Tom] Let's get back inside

1453
00:58:36,666 --> 00:58:39,135
before that kid comes back again.

1454
00:58:39,135 --> 00:58:42,635
- [Crow] No Claude Akins, but what a butt!

1455
00:58:48,562 --> 00:58:50,062
- [Joel] Mitchell.

1456
00:58:52,823 --> 00:58:53,740
- Sit down.

1457
00:58:56,228 --> 00:58:57,061
- Well--

1458
00:58:57,061 --> 00:58:58,516
- Shut up son, you don't drink do you?

1459
00:58:58,516 --> 00:59:00,816
- [Joel] Just pour, Dad.

1460
00:59:00,816 --> 00:59:03,483
- Well, this is the way it went.

1461
00:59:04,693 --> 00:59:06,278
Mistretta made this set up.

1462
00:59:06,278 --> 00:59:07,111
- [Joel] With Gallano.

1463
00:59:07,111 --> 00:59:08,543
- Gonna be too late to
tell me that the heroin

1464
00:59:08,543 --> 00:59:11,243
was on the water coming to
my operation in San Pedro.

1465
00:59:11,243 --> 00:59:13,670
Now, he tells me the stuff
is already on its way.

1466
00:59:13,670 --> 00:59:15,401
- [Joel] From Mistretta.
(Mitchell talking)

1467
00:59:15,401 --> 00:59:16,234
- Well,
- [Tom] Don't close it,

1468
00:59:16,234 --> 00:59:17,462
don't close it!

1469
00:59:17,462 --> 00:59:19,426
- Mistretta phoned a little while back.

1470
00:59:19,426 --> 00:59:20,925
- [Joel] Oh, you mean Gallano.

1471
00:59:20,925 --> 00:59:23,506
- With an ultimatum, I
have an hour to reply.

1472
00:59:23,506 --> 00:59:24,566
- What are you going to do?

1473
00:59:24,566 --> 00:59:27,421
- I'm gonna think, Mitchell.

1474
00:59:27,421 --> 00:59:28,741
Then I'm gonna call Mistretta back

1475
00:59:28,741 --> 00:59:31,681
and tell him it was okay
to use my port facilities.

1476
00:59:31,681 --> 00:59:33,082
- [Crow] Port, you've got port here?

1477
00:59:33,082 --> 00:59:35,552
- I'm gonna set it up,
hand it over to you.

1478
00:59:35,552 --> 00:59:36,503
- [Crow] Ta-da!

1479
00:59:36,503 --> 00:59:38,641
- That sounds just a
little too good to be true.

1480
00:59:38,641 --> 00:59:39,762
- It might.

1481
00:59:39,762 --> 00:59:41,185
- How's their stuff gonna come in?

1482
00:59:41,185 --> 00:59:42,933
- Well a rich woman in a big car

1483
00:59:42,933 --> 00:59:45,358
is gonna pick up the
luggage that she sent ahead

1484
00:59:45,358 --> 00:59:47,081
after her vacation in Acapulco,

1485
00:59:47,081 --> 00:59:48,566
you're gonna be the chauffeur.

1486
00:59:48,566 --> 00:59:50,072
- [Joel] Well, it's
gonna be $3.50 an hour.

1487
00:59:50,072 --> 00:59:51,599
- Your rendezvous with Mistretta.

1488
00:59:51,599 --> 00:59:53,107
- [Crow] Gallano.
- [Mitchell] Where is it?

1489
00:59:53,107 --> 00:59:55,020
- He has a house in Calabasas.

1490
00:59:55,020 --> 00:59:57,779
Now you get the heroin, you get Mistretta.

1491
00:59:57,779 --> 00:59:59,321
You don't get me, understood?

1492
00:59:59,321 --> 01:00:01,507
You don't get me.

1493
01:00:01,507 --> 01:00:03,864
- Alright, what time does
this start happening?

