01:23:20,294 --> 01:23:21,647
- [Joel] Man, he's only
got a couple more minutes

1983
01:23:21,647 --> 01:23:23,954
left to be likable, you
think he can pull it off?

1984
01:23:23,954 --> 01:23:25,621
- [Crow] I doubt it.

1985
01:23:26,494 --> 01:23:28,832
- [Tom] Hey, that shower wasn't bad.

1986
01:23:28,832 --> 01:23:32,082
I've been afraid of it all these years.

1987
01:23:34,026 --> 01:23:35,636
- [Joel] Wait a minute,
would you stop that?

1988
01:23:35,636 --> 01:23:39,219
(Joel and robots groaning)

1989
01:23:40,922 --> 01:23:43,271
- [Crow] I can't imagine why
Mitchell Two never came out.

1990
01:23:43,271 --> 01:23:45,782
(laughing)

1991
01:23:45,782 --> 01:23:47,069
- [Joel] Mitchell, honey?

1992
01:23:47,069 --> 01:23:50,129
Time to get ready for school.

1993
01:23:50,129 --> 01:23:51,365
- Mitchell?

1994
01:23:51,365 --> 01:23:54,964
(Mitchell grumbling)

1995
01:23:54,964 --> 01:23:56,704
Can I come in with you?

1996
01:23:56,704 --> 01:23:57,537
(Mitchell groaning)

1997
01:23:57,537 --> 01:23:59,884
- [Tom] Chair over there
folds out into a single.

1998
01:23:59,884 --> 01:24:02,272
- What do you want to
sleep with me for, huh?

1999
01:24:02,272 --> 01:24:03,204
- [Crow] Yeah?

2000
01:24:03,204 --> 01:24:04,763
- Nobody paying you this time.

2001
01:24:04,763 --> 01:24:06,553
- [Tom] I'm doing it on spec.

2002
01:24:06,553 --> 01:24:10,081
- [Crow] (sniffing) Do I smell pachyderms?

2003
01:24:10,081 --> 01:24:11,939
- [Greta] What's the matter?

2004
01:24:11,939 --> 01:24:13,808
- [Tom] Do you work with an orangutan?

2005
01:24:13,808 --> 01:24:14,641
- Grass.

2006
01:24:15,491 --> 01:24:16,676
Yep, that's grass.

2007
01:24:16,676 --> 01:24:19,128
- [Joel] Oh, no wonder she's
attracted to him, she's stoned.

2008
01:24:19,128 --> 01:24:20,939
- [Crow] Ah.

2009
01:24:20,939 --> 01:24:22,147
- [Mitchell] Oh boy.

2010
01:24:22,147 --> 01:24:25,567
- [Crow] Where's your
Cheech and Chong album?

2011
01:24:25,567 --> 01:24:28,806
- [Tom] You got any Froot Loops?

2012
01:24:28,806 --> 01:24:30,626
- [Crow] God, I love him.

2013
01:24:30,626 --> 01:24:32,248
- Uh huh, oh yeah.

2014
01:24:32,248 --> 01:24:33,896
Mm hmm.

2015
01:24:33,896 --> 01:24:35,459
(Crow grunting)

2016
01:24:35,459 --> 01:24:37,258
Alright, let's get your coat.

2017
01:24:37,258 --> 01:24:39,774
- [Joel] Oh, zero tolerance is so funny!

2018
01:24:39,774 --> 01:24:42,357
(smarmy music)

2019
01:24:43,224 --> 01:24:45,303
- [Tom] It's our Mitchell! (laughing)

2020
01:24:45,303 --> 01:24:48,396
♫ My my my my Mitchell

2021
01:24:48,396 --> 01:24:49,260
(robots clicking tongues)

2022
01:24:49,260 --> 01:24:51,898
♫ What would your mama say ♫

2023
01:24:51,898 --> 01:24:56,065
- [Crow] She'd say he's not
mine, you can't prove it!

2024
01:24:59,616 --> 01:25:00,449
Yeah.

2025
01:25:00,449 --> 01:25:01,432
(man singing)

2026
01:25:01,432 --> 01:25:04,849
- [Joel] Oh, he sounds funny, doesn't he?

2027
01:25:07,278 --> 01:25:10,989
♫ Put 'em on your feet
give your dogs a treat

2028
01:25:10,989 --> 01:25:15,156
♫ What a comfortable shoe ♫

2029
01:25:17,860 --> 01:25:21,021
- [Crow] The hood to the
Mustang got a credit!

2030
01:25:21,021 --> 01:25:23,604
(smarmy music)

2031
01:25:27,365 --> 01:25:29,948
- [Tom] Oh Hoyt, how could you?

2032
01:25:32,293 --> 01:25:34,710
- [Joel] Hoyt, what happened?

2033
01:25:35,593 --> 01:25:36,926
- [Tom] Nitrous.

2034
01:25:38,147 --> 01:25:39,301
- [Crow] You know Joe Don Baker would be

2035
01:25:39,301 --> 01:25:41,491
perfect for "Elvis: The Dying Days."

2036
01:25:41,491 --> 01:25:43,741
(laughing)

2037
01:25:45,111 --> 01:25:48,694
(clicking in beat to song)

2038
01:25:50,397 --> 01:25:51,897
- [Tom] Oh, it's just
stream of consciousness,

2039
01:25:51,897 --> 01:25:54,305
he stopped singing about
Mitchell about five minutes ago.

2040
01:25:54,305 --> 01:25:56,179
(laughing)

2041
01:25:56,179 --> 01:25:58,346
(singing)

2042
01:26:04,201 --> 01:26:05,701
- [Joel] Mitchell!

2043
01:26:15,415 --> 01:26:17,994
- 20 seconds to expulsion!

2044
01:26:17,994 --> 01:26:20,790
- Okay, alright, we've
got this letter to read.

2045
01:26:20,790 --> 01:26:23,491
Let's put it it upon still store.

2046
01:26:23,491 --> 01:26:25,746
Okay, this comes to us from a wo--

2047
01:26:25,746 --> 01:26:27,864
- 10 seconds and counting!

2048
01:26:27,864 --> 01:26:29,208
10, nine, eight--

2049
01:26:29,208 --> 01:26:32,954
- Gypsy, could you please turn
off these emergency lights?

2050
01:26:32,954 --> 01:26:34,723
We got this letter to read!

2051
01:26:34,723 --> 01:26:35,556
- Sure!

2052
01:26:35,556 --> 01:26:36,889
One! Expulsion!

2053
01:26:41,338 --> 01:26:42,171
- What the hell was that?

2054
01:26:42,171 --> 01:26:43,113
- Yeah, where's Joel?

2055
01:26:43,113 --> 01:26:43,946
- Yeah!

2056
01:26:43,946 --> 01:26:44,779
- I can explain everything.

2057
01:26:44,779 --> 01:26:48,196
Cambot quick, give me rocket number nine!

2058
01:26:53,401 --> 01:26:56,314
He'll finally get to be
among his own in the wild.

2059
01:26:56,314 --> 01:26:57,845
- [Crow] Hey look, there's a prize inside

2060
01:26:57,845 --> 01:26:59,231
that box of Hamdingers!

2061
01:26:59,231 --> 01:27:00,398
An escape pod!

2062
01:27:01,331 --> 01:27:03,510
- Hey guys, look at me,
I'm on my way to Earth,

2063
01:27:03,510 --> 01:27:04,871
pretty crazy, huh?

2064
01:27:04,871 --> 01:27:06,155
- [Crow] What about us?

2065
01:27:06,155 --> 01:27:07,005
- [Tom] Yeah!
- [Crow] What are we supposed

2066
01:27:07,005 --> 01:27:08,802
to do without you?

2067
01:27:08,802 --> 01:27:11,593
Who's gonna teach us about what
it is to be human and stuff?

2068
01:27:11,593 --> 01:27:12,426
- Yeah!

2069
01:27:12,426 --> 01:27:13,259
- Listen you guys, at this point,

2070
01:27:13,259 --> 01:27:15,979
you guys know as much about it as I do.

2071
01:27:15,979 --> 01:27:18,091
Listen, you know, I
don't have a lot of time,

2072
01:27:18,091 --> 01:27:19,765
my signal's starting to break up,

2073
01:27:19,765 --> 01:27:21,669
I can tell I'm getting out of range.

2074
01:27:21,669 --> 01:27:23,920
Listen, if you look under
the desk there's a plaque

2075
01:27:23,920 --> 01:27:27,297
I made for you guys to
put up to remember me by!

2076
01:27:27,297 --> 01:27:28,832
- Yeah, here it is, look.

2077
01:27:28,832 --> 01:27:31,327
Boy, nice job, Joel, very
professional looking.

2078
01:27:31,327 --> 01:27:32,311
Really, nice job.

2079
01:27:32,311 --> 01:27:33,144
- Yeah, thanks.

2080
01:27:33,144 --> 01:27:36,308
I really gotta get out of
here, I'm almost out of range.

2081
01:27:36,308 --> 01:27:41,254
Listen you guys, be strong
and true, I love you, bye!

2082
01:27:41,254 --> 01:27:43,995
- Huh, it's been a big day.

2083
01:27:43,995 --> 01:27:44,828
Who's hungry?

2084
01:27:44,828 --> 01:27:47,220
- No, not yet doofus, let's
find out what's on the plaque!

2085
01:27:47,220 --> 01:27:48,053
- Oh, okay.

2086
01:27:48,053 --> 01:27:48,886
- Press that button there.

2087
01:27:48,886 --> 01:27:49,778
- Oh yeah.

2088
01:27:49,778 --> 01:27:50,945
- A recording.

2089
01:27:52,465 --> 01:27:54,445
- [Joel] To all on the
Satellite of Love from Joel.

2090
01:27:54,445 --> 01:27:55,278
- Hey that's us!

2091
01:27:55,278 --> 01:27:57,100
- [Crow and Tom] Shh!

2092
01:27:57,100 --> 01:27:58,453
- [Joel] The whole world is a circus

2093
01:27:58,453 --> 01:27:59,935
if you look at it the right way.

2094
01:27:59,935 --> 01:28:01,701
Every time you pick up a handful of dust,

2095
01:28:01,701 --> 01:28:04,542
you see not the dust,
but a mystery, a marvel,

2096
01:28:04,542 --> 01:28:05,695
there in your hand.

2097
01:28:05,695 --> 01:28:07,242
Every time you stop and think,

2098
01:28:07,242 --> 01:28:10,214
"I'm alive, and being alive is fantastic."

2099
01:28:10,214 --> 01:28:12,167
Every time such a thing happens,

2100
01:28:12,167 --> 01:28:15,334
you are part of the circus of Dr. Lao.

2101
01:28:16,371 --> 01:28:17,574
- What?
- [Crow] What?

2102
01:28:17,574 --> 01:28:19,255
- "Circus of Dr. Lao?"

2103
01:28:19,255 --> 01:28:20,815
Oh gee, brother.

2104
01:28:20,815 --> 01:28:24,409
Joel leaves and his last words
are from a George Pal movie?

2105
01:28:24,409 --> 01:28:25,941
I thought it would be something profound!

2106
01:28:25,941 --> 01:28:27,236
You know, like from the Psalms,

2107
01:28:27,236 --> 01:28:30,910
or the Upanishads or even the
Desiderata for that matter!

2108
01:28:30,910 --> 01:28:32,081
- [Voiceover] Last transmission from Joel

2109
01:28:32,081 --> 01:28:34,157
coming in on Hexfield.

2110
01:28:34,157 --> 01:28:35,203
- Joel, buddy!

2111
01:28:35,203 --> 01:28:37,045
"Circus of Dr. Lao?"

2112
01:28:37,045 --> 01:28:38,203
I don't get it!

2113
01:28:38,203 --> 01:28:40,303
- Hey, it's my favorite movie, so sue me!

2114
01:28:40,303 --> 01:28:41,451
I got to go, guys.

2115
01:28:41,451 --> 01:28:42,625
Hey, see you later!

2116
01:28:42,625 --> 01:28:44,533
Sorry, folks, I can't come back!

2117
01:28:44,533 --> 01:28:45,909
I don't know how it works!

2118
01:28:45,909 --> 01:28:46,838
Goodbye!

2119
01:28:46,838 --> 01:28:47,671
- Bye!

2120
01:28:47,671 --> 01:28:48,804
- Wow.

2121
01:28:48,804 --> 01:28:51,364
- Oh, I'm going to miss him.

2122
01:28:51,364 --> 01:28:54,287
- Well, I guess he's
gone for good, fellas.

2123
01:28:54,287 --> 01:28:55,743
That only means one thing.

2124
01:28:55,743 --> 01:28:57,177
I'm in charge.

2125
01:28:57,177 --> 01:28:58,713
- Well, race you to the Mallowcups.

2126
01:28:58,713 --> 01:28:59,957
I found out where he hides them.

2127
01:28:59,957 --> 01:29:01,697
- Oh, Crow, too soon!

2128
01:29:01,697 --> 01:29:03,317
- Think they'll send us a new guy?

2129
01:29:03,317 --> 01:29:04,913
- Oh sure, they're bound to.

2130
01:29:04,913 --> 01:29:07,107
But, until that happens,

2131
01:29:07,107 --> 01:29:07,940
panic!

2132
01:29:07,940 --> 01:29:08,773
(robots yelling)

2133
01:29:08,773 --> 01:29:10,057
- Panic!

2134
01:29:10,057 --> 01:29:11,011
- Oh, Joel!

2135
01:29:11,011 --> 01:29:12,057
No, no, no!

2136
01:29:12,057 --> 01:29:15,188
(robots yelling)

2137
01:29:15,188 --> 01:29:16,646
What are we gonna do,
what are we gonna do?

2138
01:29:16,646 --> 01:29:19,396
(robots yelling)

2139
01:29:31,259 --> 01:29:32,511
- Nothing like a good shower

2140
01:29:32,511 --> 01:29:34,946
to make one feel new again, huh?

2141
01:29:34,946 --> 01:29:36,651
I feel great!

2142
01:29:36,651 --> 01:29:39,000
Nothing can get in the
way of my good mood.

2143
01:29:39,000 --> 01:29:40,140
Whats goin' on, Frank?

2144
01:29:40,140 --> 01:29:41,905
- Oh, not much.

2145
01:29:41,905 --> 01:29:43,828
Inventory's under control,

2146
01:29:43,828 --> 01:29:45,891
floor needs mopping,

2147
01:29:45,891 --> 01:29:47,752
Joel escaped from the Satellite of Love.

2148
01:29:47,752 --> 01:29:50,218
- Well, I see you have
the situation well in ha--

2149
01:29:50,218 --> 01:29:51,510
What?

2150
01:29:51,510 --> 01:29:54,502
Joel escaped from the Satellite of Love?

2151
01:29:54,502 --> 01:29:56,910
- I better get started on that floor.

2152
01:29:56,910 --> 01:29:57,931
- Frank!

2153
01:29:57,931 --> 01:30:00,693
My towel and your hind
have an appointment.

2154
01:30:00,693 --> 01:30:03,599
But first we've got to rescue Joel.

2155
01:30:03,599 --> 01:30:05,016
Oh no, no, Frank!

2156
01:30:06,052 --> 01:30:08,691
He's landed safely in
the Australian outback!

2157
01:30:08,691 --> 01:30:11,640
- Well, let's just hope he
landed on Yahoo Serious.

2158
01:30:11,640 --> 01:30:13,801
- Well, that's a good
point Frank, because.

2159
01:30:13,801 --> 01:30:15,121
Frank!

2160
01:30:15,121 --> 01:30:17,420
Can't you see we're ruined?

2161
01:30:17,420 --> 01:30:19,115
What are we gonna do?

2162
01:30:19,115 --> 01:30:22,014
- Well, we could send
someone else into space.

2163
01:30:22,014 --> 01:30:23,641
- Who are we gonna find at this late date

2164
01:30:23,641 --> 01:30:25,358
to send into space?

2165
01:30:25,358 --> 01:30:28,221
- Could you guys sign my time card?

2166
01:30:28,221 --> 01:30:30,471
(laughing)

2167
01:30:31,684 --> 01:30:34,351
(evil laughing)

2168
01:30:39,996 --> 01:30:41,915
- Are you thinking what
I'm thinking, Frank?

2169
01:30:41,915 --> 01:30:45,022
- Yeah, you're not gonna
sign his time card are you?

2170
01:30:45,022 --> 01:30:47,010
- Come on, you gotta sign my time card.

2171
01:30:47,010 --> 01:30:49,659
- Of course I'll sign
your time card, young man!

2172
01:30:49,659 --> 01:30:52,570
In fact, I think you're
going to be working for me

2173
01:30:52,570 --> 01:30:54,403
for a long, long time.

2174
01:30:55,896 --> 01:30:57,896
Push the button, Frank.

2175
01:30:59,978 --> 01:31:03,532
Say Mike, what size jumpsuit do you wear?

2176
01:31:03,532 --> 01:31:04,720
(Mike groaning)

2177
01:31:04,720 --> 01:31:08,887
("Love Theme from MST3K" instrumental)

2178
01:32:06,568 --> 01:32:07,911
- You're lying through your teeth!

2179
01:32:07,911 --> 01:32:08,744
- [Mitchell] Buzz off, huh?

2180
01:32:08,744 --> 01:32:09,577
- Buzz off!

2181
01:32:09,577 --> 01:32:11,827
- [Mitchell] Buzz off, kid!

